We examine the operator product expansion (OPE) of two spinning operators within the AdS$_{3}$/CFT$_{2}$ framework, focusing on the specific case where the conformal dimensions of the operators are equal. By employing the Mellin transform, we derive the explicit form of the OPE coefficient for the resulting spinning operator. Our analysis reveals that this coefficient exhibits a pole structure identical to that of the corresponding coefficient in the global conformal field theory. Furthermore, we demonstrate that the OPE coefficient for the spinning operator in AdS$_{3}$/CFT$_{2}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of the OPE coefficients for scalar operators in the same theory. Finally, we provide a detailed discussion regarding the pole structure of the OPE coefficient for spinning operators in AdS$_{3}$/CFT$_{2}$. These findings offer valuable insights into the pole structure of spinning OPE coefficients in AdS$_{d+1}$/CFT$_{d}$ theories. This work was supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China under grant No. 11975120.
